Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.799 --> 00:00:02.550 align:start position:0%
 
right dear friends  dear colleagues  i think uh let's get started we've uh  had a lot of informal discussions i  think let's uh  get on with the informal stock taking  plenary  so friends we've uh had months of vital  discussions  we've had two incredibly intense weeks  of negotiations in glasgow  and we arrive  at what i believe is the moment of truth  and this is the moment of truth  for our planet  and it's a moment of truth for our  children and our grandchildren  and you all know  that the world is willing us on to be  bold to be ambitious  and so much rest on the decisions that  we collectively take today  but you know that already  so let me start first by thanking you  once again from the bottom of my heart  for your hard work  which for some is the culmination of  several years of efforts  and i am deeply grateful to the ministry  of facilitators who have helped us to  shift gears and make progress this week  and i'd like to also like to thank my  team and of course our friends the unf  triple c sectariat for their intense  efforts to convert the fruits of  yesterday's discussions into revised  texts overnight issued under my  authority as president  these texts  are now clean  and we believe that they are the product  of a transparent inclusive and  party-driven process  and has been  founded on listening and the search for  consensus  and they've been co-created with you  they've been revised they've been tested  and they've been revised once again  now can i just say friends very candidly  that you all know the nature of these  negotiations  as presidency we have effectively had to  take into account and balance the views  of almost 200 parties  and i completely understand  that parties sometimes have different  priorities  and yet we all ultimately have to sign  up to the same agreement  i hope however that you share my view  that taken together  these latest iterations represent the  comprehensive  ambitious and balanced set of outcomes  that you can collectively that you  collectively call for in yesterday's  informal plenary and indeed in the  intense discussions which ran into the  early hours of this morning  outcomes that serve to keep within reach  the paris temperature goal of limiting  global warming to well below 2 degrees  and pursuing efforts to limit warming to  1.5 within reach  outcomes that will facilitate the rapid  scale-up of action and support on  adaptation  that lay the ground for mobilizing the  increased climate finance needed to  achieve the goals of the paris agreement  and that elevate the importance of  averting minimizing and addressing loss  and damage including through  strengthened institutional arrangements  we're all well aware that collectively  our climate ambition and action to date  have fallen short of delivering on the  promises made in paris  and importantly these texts recognized  this and set out a clear response  now  whilst many will call for that response  to go even further  these decisions i believe set out  tangible next steps and very clear  milestones to get us on track to meet  the goals of the paris agreement across  each of the three pillars of this  process mitigation adaptation and  finance  and they're guided by equity and common  but differentiated responsibilities and  respective capabilities in the light of  different national circumstances  importantly  these tests texts also provide a way  forward on the three outstanding  elements of the paris rulebook  common time frames the enhanced  transparency framework and article six  consensus on these issues friends have  evaded us for far too long  today's texts reflect the compromise  reached through the effort collaboration  and civil discourse of each and every  one of you  and once adopted they will facilitate  the full and effective implementation of  the paris agreement  these texts along with decisions already  adopted  respond to the unprecedented agenda that  we faced coming into this conference and  demonstrate that parties came to glasgow  to deliver on their mandates leaving no  issue behind  so friends we have reached a critical  juncture  where we must come together  and bring our hard work to a successful  conclusion  you're all skilled negotiators and your  committed champions of your national  interests and i respect that  and of course we are at that stage in  the negotiation when you and your  delegations may be asking yourselves  whether you can leverage this moment to  deliver more for your country for your  region or your group  and i implore you  not to  please do not ask yourself what more you  can seek  but ask instead  what is enough  is this package  balanced  does it provide enough for all of us  and you have to ask yourself  whether taken together  these texts represent a fair balance  for your government for all parties and  with progress being made on all issues  and most importantly  please ask yourselves  whether ultimately these texts deliver  for all our people  and our planet  we know that the climate crisis is a  truly global challenge  and ensuring the cop 26 outcomes  match the scale and urgency of our  situation is our shared responsibility  as i said at the start of this  conference  we will succeed or fail  as one  so i propose  that  we will shortly adjourn this informal  plenary to enable the final finalization  of documents and that we meet again this  afternoon for the final closing  plenaries of the cop the cmp and the cma  and as i said earlier  we do want to conclude this cop  this afternoon  friends the world is watching us  they're willing us to reach an agreement  here for the sake of our planet and for  present and future generations  i believe  that the texts before you deliver on the  expectations the priorities that you  have communicated to my team and to me  over the past two years and they do so  in a balanced manner leaving no issue  and no party behind  and so i invite you to join together  this afternoon to bring this collective  effort to a successful conclusion  to demonstrate that unity of purpose  that our leaders  at the start of this summit and indeed  our people across the world demand  so what i would like to propose  is that we now  adjourn this meeting

